bf16 naive matmul equals the once-narrowed wide-accumulation reference: true
the emitted serial k-loop narrows the accumulator once per cell, not per step: true
Unroll-annotated bf16 reduction keeps the wide accumulator (equals the serial result): true
materialized-unroll bf16 reduction keeps the wide accumulator (equals the serial result): true
Partition segments share one accumulator scope (equals the unsplit serial result): true
a partition segment stays addressable by later schedule ops (unrolling a segment equals the serial result): true
two-axis bf16 reduction equals the once-narrowed wide-accumulation reference: true
materialized-unrolled INNER reduction axis equals the serial result (the scope hoists through the outer reduction loop): true
materialized-unrolled OUTER reduction axis equals the serial result: true
Unroll-annotated both reduction axes equals the serial result: true
BOTH reduction axes materialized sequentially keep the whole-nest accumulator (equals the serial result): true
Pad-guarded materialized unroll equals the serial result (the guard peels into the scope): true
inner loops stay reachable after an outer materializing unroll (annotating them equals the serial result): true
a vectorized inner reduction axis folds into the whole-nest wide accumulator (equals the serial result): true
adjacent accumulations into one cell keep their per-assignment narrowing (256 +1 +1 stays 256 at bf16): true
index-guarded bf16 reduction accumulates wide across the guard (256 +1x5 narrows once to 260): true
a non-reduction recurrence through a pre-existing scope keeps its per-iteration narrowing (256 -0.5 -0.5 stays 256 at bf16): true
a Workgroup_reduce loop serialized on cc keeps the Serial accumulator width (equals the serial result): true
the SIMD reduction folds its non-divisible tail into the wide total (equals the serial result): true
narrow_compute_f32=false recovers per-operator rounding: the result differs from the widened default: true
narrow_compute_f32=false brings back the per-k-step narrowing in the k-loop: true
